nodecode-proof-run is a rewrite of raffieeey's raffieeey/hermes-proof-run:

  https://github.com/raffieeey/hermes-proof-run
  commit 36f3f4111b6d8cd5cf67d53eaf54e62148fcf3ca
  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 raffieeey (LICENSE)

Rewritten: the plugin's three Hermes hooks and its Python modules as one
Nodecode cell. The pre_tool_call gate and the post_tool_call observer become
one :TOOL point hook over the dispatch, which sees a call before its body runs
and the answer after; the /proof command becomes /proof-run with the same
verbs (start, stop, cancel, learn, rebind, status, unbind); the observed-step
contract, the exact-argument comparison, the read preconditions with their
age, the consumption of a read by the next mutation, the unproven verdict and
the profile-wide saved contract are kept, as a JSON file per contract under
the Nodecode home. The matcher is reimplemented in Common Lisp with no
dependencies, and a proof_status tool lets the model read what is gating.

Left out, and why: the version history directory beside each contract, since a
rebind overwrites the file at version + 1; the descriptor-relative no-follow
storage dance and the per-name flock, because Nodecode writes one file
atomically through its own home and a cell is one process; the legacy
version-1 schema and its rebind refusal, because nothing here ever wrote one;
the credential scan over the contract text, which is one keyword sweep over
the arguments instead; and the Hermes tool-name table of read-only tools,
which is a section list here, because in Nodecode almost every call is the
eval tool and a read is a verb inside its form.
